>
<h1>Custom Conveyor Design Guide</h1>
<p class="usa-intro">Custom conveyor design makes sense when catalog conveyors cannot meet your requirements for product geometry, environment, throughput, or integration constraints. Custom builds cost 30–100% more than standard models and take 8–20 weeks to deliver, but they eliminate the compromises and workaround engineering that come from forcing a standard product into a non-standard application. This guide explains when custom is justified, what the design process looks like from inquiry to commissioning, what information <a href="/resources/conveyor-manufacturers/">manufacturers</a> need to provide an accurate quote, and how to manage <a href="/resources/conveyor-cost-guide/">cost</a> and risk on custom projects.</p>
<h2 id="vs-heading">Custom vs. Catalog: When Each Makes Sense</h2>
<p>Most conveyor manufacturers offer three tiers of product: catalog (standard), modified standard, and full custom. Understanding where your application falls saves time in the quoting process and sets realistic expectations for cost and lead time.</p>
